---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { u, getScorecards } from '../lib/data.mjs';

const cards = getScorecards();

// Replication is the only trust mechanism here that does not require believing us. It needs no
// consensus, no votes and no honest-majority assumption: two machines either derive the same hash
// from the same public snapshot or they do not, and a disagreement is a bug report.
const CROWD_CAN = [
  'Run a replica: snapshot the same sources, compute scorecards with the same published code, publish a signed hash.',
  'Propose an anchor for a domain, with its provenance and settle rule, by pull request.',
  'Contribute a catalog entry, or a quirk report about a feed you know better than we do.',
  'Propose a method change, as an ADR, versioned, applying to every source at once.',
  'File a dispute with a reproduction attached.',
];

const CROWD_CANNOT = [
  'Vote on a score. Popularity is not a measurement, and every benchmark that let the crowd vote was captured.',
  'Set or adjust a number by hand, including their own.',
  'Bypass review on a catalog entry or a license citation.',
  'Change the method for one source without changing it for all of them.',
  'File a dispute without a reproduction.',
];
---

<Layout title="Replication">
  <div style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Replication</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 820px;">
      A benchmark you have to trust is not a benchmark. The intended check on this project is not our promise of
      independence, it is that someone else runs the same code over the same public snapshots and gets the same
      bytes. Two machines either agree on a hash or they do not.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section style="border: 1px solid #fcd34d; background: #fffbeb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; color: #78350f;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">State today: zero replicas, and it is not yet possible to run one</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
      The scoring code is not public yet. The core repository is private by an accepted decision (ADR-0006), which
      also commits to publishing the verification logic, the schemas, and the catalog as a companion public
      repository. That companion has not shipped. Until it does, nobody outside this project can recompute a card,
      <code>make reproduce</code> is a command only we can run, and every independence claim on this site rests on
      our word.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 0.95rem;">
      That is a gap between what this project says about itself and what it can currently demonstrate, and it is
      stated here rather than left for a reader to discover. Publishing the verifier is the work that closes it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">What a replica is</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      An independent operator, on their own host, doing the whole job: snapshotting the same sources on the same
      declared cadence, running the published scoring code, and publishing the resulting digests. The signal is
      agreement between replicas that share no infrastructure.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th style="width: 13rem;">Step</th><th>What it proves</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Recompute from our archive</strong></td>
          <td>The code does what the method page says. Same snapshots in, byte-identical card out. This catches a scoring bug and a fudged number equally well.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Snapshot independently</strong></td>
          <td>The archive itself is honest. A replica that captures the same feeds on its own schedule can compare what it saw against what we recorded, which is the only real check on an append-only archive nobody else witnessed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Publish an attestation</strong></td>
          <td>The comparison is on the record: which snapshot, which method version, which digest, and whether it matched. A disagreement becomes a bug report with evidence rather than an argument.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">What a replica attestation says</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
      The shape below is the target, not something published yet. It is here so it can be argued with before it
      exists rather than after.
    </p>
    <pre>{`{
  "replica_id":      "who ran it, and where",
  "subject":         { "type": "scorecard", "source_id": "nws" },
  "method_version":  "0.2",
  "as_of":           "2026-09-13T22:00:04Z",
  "snapshot_digest": "sha256 of the inputs it scored",
  "result_digest":   "sha256 of the card it produced",
  "matches_origin":  true,
  "signed_at":       "2026-09-14T00:00:00Z"
}`}</pre>
    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 820px;">
      <code>matches_origin: false</code> is the interesting record, and the one that has to survive publication. A
      replica that only publishes its agreements is decoration.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">What the crowd can and cannot do</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      Replication is the decentralisation this project wants. It needs no tokens, no consensus mechanism, and no
      assumption that most participants are honest, because the check is arithmetic rather than a vote.
    </p>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem;">
      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-top: 4px solid #15803d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.1rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Anyone can</h3>
        <ul style="margin-left: 1.1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.92rem;">
          {CROWD_CAN.map((row) => <li>{row}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-top: 4px solid #b91c1c; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.1rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Nobody can</h3>
        <ul style="margin-left: 1.1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.92rem;">
          {CROWD_CANNOT.map((row) => <li>{row}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">The known replicas</h2>
    <div style="border: 1px dashed var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-subtle);">
      <p style="font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">None. One operator, one host, {cards.length} cards.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
        The target is three replicas on three hosts, at least one of them not operated by us. When one exists it is
        listed here with its attestations, agreements and disagreements alike. If replicas ever disagree and the
        cause is not found to be a bug, scorecard publication stops until it is: an unreproducible method is not a
        method.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">What you can check right now</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
      Short of a replica, the published artifacts are still checkable by hand: every band edge is on the
      <a href={u('/protocols')}>protocols page</a>, so any letter grade can be re-derived from the measured value
      printed beside it, and every emblem resolves to the claim it made on the <a href={u('/trace')}>trace ledger</a>.
      Those checks catch a mislabelled grade. They do not catch a wrong measurement, which is what a replica is for.
    </p>
    <pre>{`curl -s https://modafied.org/v1/scorecards/nws.json | jq '{method_version, dimensions}'
curl -s https://modafied.org/v1/ratings/nws.json   | jq '.composite'`}</pre>
  </section>
</Layout>
